### -------------------------------------------
### KHMCRAFT API TESTING FILE
### You can use the "REST Client" extension in VS Code to click "Send Request" directly from this file!
### -------------------------------------------

### 1. Submit a Seller Application
POST http://localhost:3001/api/sellers/apply
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Sokha",
  "lastName": "Lim",
  "phoneNumber": "+85512345678",
  "province": "Phnom Penh",
  "primaryCategory": "Weaving"
}

###

### 2. Get All Seller Applications
GET http://localhost:3001/api/sellers/apply

###

### 3. Register an Approved Seller
POST http://localhost:3001/api/sellers/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sokha Lim",
  "email": "sokha@khmercraft.com",
  "password": "mysecurepassword123",
  "storeName": "Sokha's Traditional Weaving",
  "storeDescription": "Preserving the art of Cambodian silk."
}

###

### 4. Login as Seller (Gets JWT Token)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/sellers/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sokha@khmercraft.com",
  "password": "mysecurepassword123"
}

###

### 5. Get all Approved Sellers (Stores)
GET http://localhost:3001/api/sellers/stores

###

### 6. Create a Product (PROTECTED - Requires Token from step 4)
# Copy the token string from the login response and replace <PASTE_TOKEN_HERE>
POST http://localhost:3001/api/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_TOKEN_HERE>

{
  "title": "Beautiful Silk Scarf",
  "price": 45.00,
  "category": "Weaving",
  "images": ["https://example.com/scarf.jpg"]
}

###

### 7. Fetch all Products
GET http://localhost:3001/api/products
